\title{Universal Property of the Product Topology}
\taxon{Proposition}
\import{macros}
\p{
    Let #{X=\prod_{i\in I}X_i} carry the [product topology](def-005V), with
    projections #{\pi_i:X\to X_i}. A map #{f:Z\to X} is continuous if and
    only if every coordinate map #{\pi_i\circ f:Z\to X_i} is continuous.
}
\proof{
    If #{f} is continuous, each coordinate map is continuous because the
    projections are continuous. Conversely, suppose all coordinate maps are
    continuous. Every basic open subset of #{X} can be written as
    ##{
        B=\bigcap_{k=1}^{n}\pi_{i_k}^{-1}(U_{i_k}),
    }
    where each #{U_{i_k}} is open in #{X_{i_k}}. Therefore
    ##{
        f^{-1}(B)
        =\bigcap_{k=1}^{n}(\pi_{i_k}\circ f)^{-1}(U_{i_k}),
    }
    a finite intersection of open subsets of #{Z}. The
    [basis criterion](thm-001C) now shows that #{f} is continuous.
}
